Subject: [PATCH] Fix linked-window White Stop state desynchronization

Diagnosis: H3 was correct. The backend emitted each craidd:build event to the
correct WebviewWindow label, but the frontend subscribed with the module-level
event.listen(), whose default target is Any. In a live two-window reproduction,
both workspace-1 and workspace-2 received start events for session 1 and
session 2, and both stores ended up with activeId=2. Cancelling one runner was
therefore either ignored by both stores or accepted by both stores depending on
which session was stopped. The same unscoped subscription affected linked
snapshots, linked commands, and debug state.

The fix subscribes through the current WebviewWindow so Tauri filters events at
the listener boundary before they can mutate another window's stores. A live
replay showed CS2 become cancelled while CS1 remained running and Gold Stop
remained active. The routing regression test guards the scoped-listener contract.

